[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    graph TD

      %% Top states
      Startup(["Startup"])
      Crash(["Crash<br/>disable HV<br/>disable emission<br/>set outputs to 0<br/>stop cooler/pumps<br/>stop indicators"])

      %% Core states
      Cold(["Cold<br/>disable HV<br/>disable emission<br/>outputs to 0<br/>stop cooling"])
      Conditioning(["Conditioning<br/>verify estops<br/>set heater<br/>start cooling"])
      Warmup(["Warmup<br/>enable fast warmup<br/>set heater<br/>start cooling"])
      WarmupFault(["Warmup Fault<br/>heater = 0<br/>stop cooling"])

      Fault(["Fault<br/>disable HV<br/>disable emission<br/>shutdown outputs"])
      ColdFault(["Cold Fault<br/>disable HV<br/>outputs to 0"])

      %% Plan pipeline
      Primed[[Primed]]
      Staging[[Staging]]
      Staged[[Staged]]

      %% Execution pipeline
      HVPSCheck(["HVPS Check<br/>disable HV<br/>disable emission"])
      Setup(["Setup<br/>enable HV<br/>set KV / grid / coils"])
      Ready(["Ready<br/>emission disabled"])
      Launching(["Launching<br/>emission disabled"])
      Emission(["Emission<br/>emission enabled"])
      Termination(["Termination<br/>shutdown safely"])

      %% Discharge
      Discharge(["Discharge<br/>HV off<br/>outputs = 0"])

      %% Startup transitions
      Startup --> Cold
      Crash --> Cold

      %% Cold transitions
      Cold -->|PC CONDITION| Conditioning
      Cold -->|PC WARMUP| Warmup
      Cold -->|FAULT| ColdFault
      Cold -->|PC WIPE PLAN| Cold
      Cold -->|PC STOP| Cold

      %% Conditioning
      Conditioning -->|HVPS SP REACHED| Primed
      Conditioning -->|FAULT| Cold

      %% Warmup
      Warmup -->|HVPS SP REACHED| Primed
      Warmup -->|FAULT| WarmupFault

      WarmupFault --> Cold

      %% Fault handling
      Fault --> Cold
      ColdFault --> Cold

      %% Plan handling
      Primed -->|PC NEW SESSION| Staging
      Staging -->|PC FINISH STAGE| Staged
      Staging -->|PC WIPE PLAN| Cold

      Staged -->|PC RELEASE PLAN| HVPSCheck

      %% HVPS / Setup
      HVPSCheck -->|Check done| Setup
      Setup -->|HVPS SP REACHED| Ready

      %% Ready → emission flow
      Ready -->|PC RELEASE POINT| Launching
      Launching -->|HVPS SP REACHED| Emission

      %% Emission loop
      Emission -->|OP COMPLETE| Ready

      %% Stop / termination
      Ready -->|PC STOP| Termination
      Emission -->|PC STOP| Termination
      Launching -->|PC STOP| Termination

      Termination --> Cold

      %% Discharge path
      Ready -->|PC STANDBY| Discharge
      Discharge --> Cold

    </pre>
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
.. raw:: html

    <pre class="mermaid">
    sequenceDiagram
        participant User
        participant Internal_GUI
        participant External_GUI
        participant GUI_Either
        participant Boards
        participant HVPS

        GUI_Either->>Boards: Initialize (startup only)

        alt Conditioning required
            GUI_Either->>Internal_GUI: Conditioning required
            Internal_GUI->>GUI_Either: Condition request
            GUI_Either->>Boards: Condition (setpoint)

            Boards->>HVPS: Ramp heater to conditioning setpoint
            HVPS-->>Boards: Filament feedback (setpoint reached)
            Boards->>HVPS: Ramp heater down to 0
            Boards-->>GUI_Either: Returned to COLD state
        end

        User->>Internal_GUI: Create plan and load
        Internal_GUI->>External_GUI: Send plan information
        External_GUI-->>User: Plan loaded

        User->>External_GUI: Execute treatment (prepare)
        External_GUI->>Boards: Warmup (setpoint)

        Boards->>HVPS: Ramp heater to warmup setpoint
        HVPS-->>Boards: Filament feedback (setpoint reached)
        Boards-->>External_GUI: Warmup complete (PRIMED)

        External_GUI->>Boards: New session command
        Boards-->>External_GUI: Session ID (STAGING)

        loop foreach operational point
            External_GUI->>Boards: Send point info
        end

        External_GUI->>Boards: Stage plan command
        Boards-->>External_GUI: Plan staged (STAGED)

        loop foreach operational point
            External_GUI->>Boards: Confirm point info
        end

        External_GUI->>Boards: Release plan command

        Boards->>HVPS: Ramp HV
        HVPS-->>Boards: HV ramp feedback (HV reached)
        Boards-->>External_GUI: READY state

        External_GUI-->>User: Ready to start emission
        User->>External_GUI: Start emission
        External_GUI->>Boards: Release point command

        loop foreach operational point
            Boards->>HVPS: Run emission
        end
    </pre>
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main Modules

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
State Machine - The routine at the heart of the Main Control Firmware operation. It processes queued events from various data sources to change the operating state of the system's functionality.

HVPS monitoring - monitors and controls data to and from the High Voltage Power Supply.

Headboard communication - monitors and controls data via UART to and from the Headboard.

PC Communication - Connects to the PC application receive commands and to transmit telemetry status data. Utilizes LWIP protocol and connects via Ethernet. Bootloader commands are connected by USB

Interlocks - safety switches that must be engaged for the system to operate properly. If any interlock is disengaged at any time, then the system will either not start or enter a fault state. Emission will also be terminated when disengaged. The user will have to correctly engage the interlock and begin again via the PC Application.

Timers - The Main Control has an internal timer and two external timers for redundancy. These timers are engaged during X-Ray emissions and are primarily for safety.

Cooling System Control - The system utilizes cabinet fans, cooling pump, and a Peltier cooler to keep the system temperature from exceeding specified limits. Temperature sensors create feedback loop with fan speed adjustment and the system cooling.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H1FWMC-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-173
TITLE: Manufacturer Hardware Abstraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware integrates source code provided by the manufacturer of the microcontroller unit to interface with various peripherals of the microcontroller. These include functions to interface with the following peripherals of the microcontroller:

- UART serial port
- SPI serial port
- I2C serial port
- GPIO
- Flash memory controller
- Timer peripheral
- Ethernet MAC peripheral
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-39
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-174
TITLE: LWIP Middleware
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware integrates the source code for a middleware library called LWIP. The version of LWIP integrated is version 1.4.1. This middleware serves to help process incoming data from and outgoing data to the Ethernet MAC peripheral, which is used to communicate with the PC. The specific LWIP functionality utilized is the UDP processing. While LWIP can perform TCP communication, only UDP is utilized.

The configuration for used for LWIP in firmware is a static IP address with a fixed MAC address. UDP communication is configured for two fixed ports.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-84
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-175
TITLE: Input Signals
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware applies the SAME70 hardware debounce/glitch filter to every physical Port C
interlock input and samples:

- Door, base e-stop, and remote e-stop status
- KUKA 1 and KUKA 2 readiness
- Water level, ion-pump, timer 1, timer 2, HVPS, cooler, water-temperature, and watchdog status
- MCU fault, spare interlocks 1 and 2, and buffered master-fault status
- Remote-key and base-key status

Port C bit 17 is not an interlock input and is excluded from sampling.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-8
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-176
TITLE: Output Signals
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware controls several digital output signals. The functionality for the output signals are as follows:

- LED control for on-board debug LEDs
- Watchdog IC control
- Fault pulse clear signal
- Ion pump enable
- Emission indicator enable
- Timer start signal
- Fan and pump enable signals
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-7
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-53
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-177
TITLE: External ADC Communication
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware communicates with three external ADC IC chips: two ADS7828 chips and one MAX11647 chips. It communicates with all three chips on a singular I2C bus. The external ADC module cycles through each channel on each chip one by one, reading in the values sent by the chips. These values are 'raw ADC' values sent to the system parameter processing for conversion to their corresponding physical units.

The I2C communication with the ADC ICs is performed using the manufacturer provided 'HRI' library or hardware register interface. This HRI library is used to set up interrupt-based communication on the I2C bus instead of having blocking commands wait for completion of writes and reads of the I2C bus which are relatively long in duration compared to the processing speed of the main microcontroller unit.

In case anyone external IC does not respond, the I2C bus is monitored for any NACK values indicating a non-response. The firmware will report a fault if no response is detected from one of the ADC ICs.

The two ADS7828 chips each have 8 channels, while the MAX11647 has two channels. One ADS7828 chip samples the feedback values from the coil control board. The other ADS7828 samples ion pump feedback, temperature sensors, and onboard power supplies. MAX11647 chip samples the ion Repeller monitoring.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
