[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-188
TITLE: General System Monitoring: Fan Control
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will continuously check at periodic intervals, various measured and reported temperature feedback signals to adjust output fan speed settings.

The cabinet fans are adjusted based on the cabinet temperature sensor feedback, with higher temperatures corresponding to higher fan speeds. The cabinet temperature change is relatively slow, and as such no hysteresis implementation is needed.

The heatsink fan is adjusted based on the heatsink temperature sensor feedback, with higher temperatures corresponding to higher fan speeds. The heatsink temperature change is relatively fast, and as such a hysteresis functionality is also implemented in the fan speed adjustment to prevent frequent oscillation of the fan speed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-63
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-65
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-189
TITLE: General System Monitoring: System Faults
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will continuously check at periodic intervals, various measured and reported feedback signals and statuses of the system to detect faults. If any issues are detected, a fault condition may be thrown away. The following are monitored conditions for fault reporting:

- Communication timeout with the PC
- Interlock fault
- Ion Repeller overcurrent and out of tolerance voltage readings
- Cooling system pressure overload
- Cooling system over temperature
- Cooling system experiencing insufficient or excessive flow.
- Heatsink over temperature
- Deflection or focus coil out of tolerance feedback
<<<
