[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-192
TITLE: State: Cold Fault
STATEMENT: >>>
The cold fault state is for when a system error has occurred, but the system does not have the filament running. The firmware can transition out of the cold fault state and into the cold state after receiving a reset fault command from the PC.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-33
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-193
TITLE: State: Conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The conditioning state is for when the system is slowly ramping up the filament current to 'condition' the source. Conditioning completes once the reported filament value from the HVPS interface board reaches the target filament current. The firmware will transition the system back to cold state once that target setpoint has been reached. Alternatively, if the PC sends a stop command, the firmware will also transition back to the cold state. If a fault occurs during the conditioning state, the system will instead transition to the warmup fault state.
<<<
