  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-37
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-194
TITLE: State: Warmup
STATEMENT: >>>
The warmup state is for when the system is ramping up the filament current to reach a level where the filament is at a temperature that can sustain lower levels of emission. Due to the nature of the HVPS filament control (constant current) and the system characteristics (increased resistance with increased temperature), and the nature of the filament and cathode sensitivity, it is not advisable to go to a higher current which could sustain the intended target levels of emission output.

Warmup completes once the reported filament value from the HVPS interface board stabilizes at the target filament current. The firmware will transition to primed state once that target setpoint has been reached if no current plan is loaded, otherwise it will transition to the staged state.

If the PC sends a stop command in the warmup state, the firmware will transition back to the cold state. If a fault occurs during the warmup state, the system will instead transition to the warmup fault state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-41
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-76
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-195
TITLE: State: Warmup Fault
STATEMENT: >>>
The warmup fault state is for when a system error has occurred when warming up the filament such as during the conditioning state or the warmup state. The firmware can transition out of the warmup fault state and into the cold state after receiving a reset fault command from the PC.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-13
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-22
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-196
TITLE: State: Primed
STATEMENT: >>>
The primed state is for when the filament of the system is at the warmup value, but no plan is loaded, nor has any plan loading been initiated. On an error, the system enters fault state. On a standby event, which can be initiated by the PC or after a timeout, the firmware transitions from primed state to discharge state. If the firmware receives a new session command in primed, it will begin a new session and transition the state into the staging state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-42
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-197
TITLE: State: Staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The staging state is for when the PC is actively loading the parameters for a new treatment plan. On an error, the system enters fault state. On a standby event, which can be initiated by the PC or after a timeout, the firmware transitions from the staging state to discharge state. If the firmware receives a wipe plan command, it will transition the state back to primed. If the PC sends a command to finalize the staging of the plan, the firmware will transition the state from staging to staged.
<<<
