[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-198
TITLE: State: Staged
STATEMENT: >>>
The staged state is for when the PC has completed a loading of a plan but has yet to release the plan for execution. Before the release of the plan is allowed, the PC must confirm all the operational points which have been loaded into the current treatment plan.

On an error, the system enters fault state. On a standby event, which can be initiated by the PC or after a timeout, the firmware transitions from the staged state to discharge state. If the firmware receives a wipe plan command, it will transition the state back to primed. If the firmware receives a valid plan release command once all the points have been confirmed, the system is transitioned into the HVPS check state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-26
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-74
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-199
TITLE: State: HVPS Check
STATEMENT: >>>
The HVPS check state is when the main application firmware performs an interlock check with the HVPS interface board. The firmware sends commands to the HVPS interface board indicating that it is going to toggle the interlocks and then toggles the interlocks. This process is to have the HVPS interface board 'unlock' the HVPS functionality to turn on high voltage and control the grid by verifying that interlocks function appropriately and can be toggled. The HVPS interface board will update its status accordingly on whether the unlock sequence was successful.

On a successful HVPS check state after toggling the interlocks, the firmware transitions into the setup state. On an error, the firmware transitions to the fault state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-21
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-200
TITLE: State: Setup
STATEMENT: >>>
The setup state is for when the firmware is ramping up the high voltage to the intended setpoint for an operational point, as well as setting the backup timers. On an error, the system enters fault state. Otherwise, if the system reaches the target high voltage output for the operational point, the firmware will transition into the ready state. If the PC sends a stop command, the firmware will instead transition to the termination state.
<<<
