- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-14
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-19
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-20
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-201
TITLE: State: Ready
STATEMENT: >>>
The ready state is for when the system has high voltage ramped up to the target setpoint for the operational point but has not yet begun emission. On an error the firmware transitions to the fault state. If the firmware receives a stop command from the PC, it will transition to the termination state. If the firmware receives a standby command, either through the PC or via a timeout, it will transition to the discharge state. If the firmware receives a release point command, it will transition into the launching state.

In the ready state if the current operational point is indicated for automatic execution, the firmware will self-request a release point command for automatic point execution. Otherwise, the PC must send the release point command.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-17
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-18
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-202
TITLE: State: Launching
STATEMENT: >>>
The launching state is for the system to ramp up the filament current so that the cathode is warm enough for targeted emission output. The firmware also sets the deflection and focusing coil outputs in this state. If an error occurs, the firmware transitions into fault state. If the PC sends a stop command, the firmware transitions to termination state. Otherwise, once the filament current has stabilized at the target current, the firmware transitions into the emission state.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-16
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-70
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-203
TITLE: State: Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The emission state is when the system is performing radiation emission output. On an error, the system enters fault state. If the PC sends a stop command, the firmware will transition to the termination state.

If the system completes the execution of the operational point without interruption, which is marked by the expiration of the operational point's target treatment time, then the firmware will either go to the termination state if it is the last operational point in the treatment plan, or it will go to the setup state to prepare for the next operational point in the treatment plan.
<<<
