[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-204
TITLE: State: Termination
STATEMENT: >>>
The termination state is for the system to ramp down high voltage and turn off the coil outputs after the termination of a treatment plan or operational point. The termination state, however, maintains the filament current value at the targeted warmup setpoint. On an error, the system enters fault state. Otherwise, once termination of the high voltage is completed, the firmware transitions to the staged state. The firmware transitions to this state as a plan still loaded, even if the loaded treatment plan has already been fully completed.
<<<
