[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-207
TITLE: System Status (Telemetry)
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware collects monitored values in a system-status array used as the source of truth
for firmware decisions and telemetry serialization. Every 10 ms, it serializes the array
using the normal or calibration layout selected at compile time and sends it to the CNC.
The normal and calibration telemetry layouts append the raw state-dependent required-interlock
mask and publish the complete physical interlock-input mask. The normal layout includes a
reserved word between the second magnetometer vector and setpoint fields so its established
payload count and field positions remain unchanged. Telemetry requests use the same serializers.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-83
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-208
TITLE: Treatment Plan (Operational Points)
STATEMENT: >>>
Each treatment plan is stored in memory as an array of operational points. The firmware will execute each operational point in the sequence in which they are stored in the array. The operational points are stored based on the index value provided when the PC sends over the operational point data.

Each operational point is a collection of fields representing the emission. These fields are the operational point index within the treatment plan, the total treatment time of the point, the remaining treatment time of the point, the high voltage kV of the point, the target emission current mA of the point, the initial filament current of the point, the X, Y and focus coil current values of the point, and whether or not the point should be auto-executed by firmware.
<<<
