[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-296
TITLE: HVPS Monitoring: Faults
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will continuously check at periodic intervals, various measured and reported HVPS feedback signals to monitor for faults. If any issues are detected, a fault condition may emerge. The following are monitored conditions for fault reporting:

- kV present when no kV should be present
- kV out of tolerance when kV should be present
- mA present when no mA should be present
- mA out of tolerance when mA should be present
- Filament overcurrent
- Occurrence of timeouts when waiting for HVPS values to stabilize
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-12
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-68
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-297
TITLE: HVPS Monitoring: Stabilization
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware will continuously check at periodic intervals, various measured and reported HVPS feedback signals to determine if the HVPS is stable at certain states. This determination of stability allows the progression of the state machine in the following states under the following conditions:

- Completion of the conditioning state by having the filament current reach the target filament current
- Completion of the warmup state by having the filament current reach the target filament current
- Completion of the setup state by having the high voltage reach the target kV
- Completion of the launching state by having the high voltage reach the target filament current
- Completion of the discharge state by having low high voltage and filament current
- Completion of the termination state by having low high voltage
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-21
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-71
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-298
TITLE: Fault Clearing
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control board has hardware which latches fault conditions and disables interlocks
so that emission is safely terminated and cannot be resumed until action is taken by the
firmware. On a PC clear-fault request, the firmware pulses the hardware clear output,
increments the software clear epoch, empties the latched fault-record table, clears the
software category flags, and publishes an empty fault update. The firmware cannot override
an active hardware fault; any remaining condition re-latches the interlocks and can create
a new software fault record.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-78
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMC-79
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMC-299
TITLE: External Watchdog
STATEMENT: >>>
The main control board contains an external watchdog IC which can terminate emission. The firmware must send a periodically toggle digital output signal and reset the watchdog IC at least once per second, or the watchdog IC will terminate the emission.
<<<
